        <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8 leading-tight">How Much Does AI Automation Cost in Australia? (2026 Pricing Guide)</h1>
        <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none font-sans text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          
          <p>One of the most common questions we get from Australian business owners is: <strong>how much does AI automation actually cost?</strong> The honest answer is that it depends enormously on what you're automating, how complex your existing systems are, and whether you're buying off-the-shelf tools or commissioning custom-built agents.</p>
          <p>This guide breaks down real pricing ranges for the most common AI automation use cases in Australia in 2026, based on what we see in the market and what we charge at PresciaIQ.</p>
          <h2>The Three Tiers of AI Automation</h2>
          <p>AI automation for Australian businesses generally falls into three tiers, each with a different cost profile and capability ceiling.</p>
          <h3>Tier 1: No-Code Workflow Automation ($0–$500/month)</h3>
          <p>Tools like Zapier, Make (formerly Integromat), and n8n allow you to connect your existing software — CRM, email, accounting — without writing a line of code. These are excellent for simple, rule-based tasks: when a new lead comes in from your website, add them to HubSpot and send a welcome email. Pricing for these platforms starts free and scales to around $200–$500/month for business-level plans with higher task volumes.</p>
          <p>The limitation is that these tools are rule-based, not intelligent. They can move data between systems, but they can't read a PDF, understand context, or make decisions based on nuanced information.</p>
          <h3>Tier 2: AI-Enhanced Automation ($500–$3,000/month)</h3>
          <p>This tier adds a layer of AI intelligence on top of workflow automation. Examples include AI email triage (where an LLM reads incoming emails and routes them to the right person), AI-powered document extraction (reading invoices and pushing structured data to Xero), and AI customer support agents trained on your knowledge base. Pricing in this tier typically ranges from $500 to $3,000 per month depending on volume and complexity, or $5,000–$20,000 as a one-time build fee for a custom implementation.</p>
          <h3>Tier 3: Custom AI Agents ($15,000–$80,000+ project fee)</h3>
          <p>Custom AI agents are purpose-built systems that can reason, take multi-step actions, and integrate deeply with your business logic. A custom agent might handle the entire inbound sales qualification process — reading a lead's website, scoring their fit, drafting a personalised outreach email, and booking a call in your calendar. These projects typically cost $15,000–$80,000 to build, with ongoing hosting and maintenance costs of $500–$2,000/month.</p>
          <h2>What PresciaIQ Charges for AI Automation</h2>
          <p>At PresciaIQ, we operate on a <strong>fixed project fee model</strong> — no ongoing retainers. Our AI automation projects typically range from $8,000 to $45,000 depending on the number of integrations, the complexity of the AI logic, and whether we're building from scratch or extending existing systems. We support 100+ software integrations and specialise in Australian business stacks: Xero, MYOB, HubSpot, Salesforce, ServiceM8, Simpro, and AroFlo.</p>
          <h2>The ROI Question</h2>
          <p>The more useful question is not "what does it cost?" but "what does it return?" A $12,000 AI automation project that eliminates 20 hours of manual data entry per week, at a fully-loaded cost of $50/hour, pays for itself in 12 weeks. A $25,000 customer support agent that handles 60% of inbound enquiries without human intervention can save a business $80,000+ per year in support staff costs.</p>
          <p>If you want a specific ROI calculation for your business, <a href="/start" class="text-primary hover:underline">book a free scoping call</a> and we'll map it out with you.</p>
          <h2>Questions to Ask Before You Buy</h2>
          <p>Before engaging any AI automation provider, ask these questions: Does the pricing include integration with your existing software stack? Who owns the code and the AI model at the end of the project? What happens when the AI makes a mistake — is there a human review step? What are the ongoing hosting and maintenance costs? A reputable provider will answer all of these clearly.</p>
        
